The rule to remember

Cart = what the customer wants to buy.

Coupon API = calculate/validate a promotion against the current cart.

Order = permanent record of the final transaction.

OrderItem = permanent record of exactly how each product was priced/discounted.

And never use the Cart's totalPrice or the frontend's discount as the final authority. The POST /orders backend should recalculate the final numbers from database data and the submitted coupon code.

That is the architecture I would use for a production-oriented multi-vendor MERN marketplace.


